<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Brahman dynasty of Sindh</h1><p class="st-meta">632 CE – 712 CE (approx.) · capital Aror</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The last Hindu dynasty of Sindh, whose king Dahir fell in 712 to the Arab army of Muhammad ibn Qasim.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>According to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chach-nama">Chach Nama</a>, a 13th-century Persian history, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-chach">Chach</a>, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmins">Brahmin</a> chamberlain at the court of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/rai-dynasty">Rai dynasty</a>, married the widowed queen after the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rai-sahasi-ii">Rai Sahasi II</a> and seized the throne at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aror">Aror</a> around 632. He spent his reign subduing rebellious governors and fixing the borders of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindh">Sindh</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chach-nama">Chach Nama</a> describes a kingdom divided into provinces under governors, with a strong Buddhist population, many monasteries and powerful <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jats">Jat</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lohana">Lohana</a> groups in the countryside. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-chach">Chach</a> was succeeded by his brother Chandar and then by his sons, of whom <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raja-dahir">Dahir</a> ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aror">Aror</a> while his brother held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmanabad">Brahmanabad</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindh">Sindh's</a> ports, such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/debal">Debal</a>, were active in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean-trade">Indian Ocean trade</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After attacks on Arab ships near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/debal">Debal</a>, the Umayyad governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-hajjaj-ibn-yusuf">al-Hajjaj</a>, sent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ibn-qasim">Muhammad ibn Qasim</a>, who took Debal in 711 and defeated and killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raja-dahir">Dahir</a> in 712. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindh">Sindh</a> became a province of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a>, and later the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/habbari-dynasty">Habbari dynasty</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/emirate-of-multan">Emirate of Multan</a> arose there.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/brahman-dynasty-of-sindh.jpg" alt="Brahman dynasty of Sindh" width="320" height="296"><figcaption>Image: Map created from DEMIS Mapserver, which are public domain. Koba-chan. Reference: [1] · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_the_Chachas_circa_650_CE.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>632 CE – 712 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Aror</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Chach, Chandar, Dahir</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism, Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Sindhi Prakrit, Sanskrit</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/pakistan">Pakistan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Chacha dynasty, Kingdom of Raja Dahir</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=672&amp;focus=brahman-dynasty-of-sindh" aria-label="Brahman dynasty of Sindh on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6491 1164 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Brahman dynasty of Sindh lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6811 1420L6811 1420M6811 1420L6134 1224"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6811 1420h0M6134 1224h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6811 1420h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6811 1420h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Aror. <a href="/atlas?year=672&amp;focus=brahman-dynasty-of-sindh">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
